From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] j604: add the J604 speaker graph and microphone

The J604 (MacBook Pro 14", M4, 2024) has six SN012776 amps, two woofers
and a tweeter per side, and a three-microphone high-power array. Apple
drives its speakers exactly as it drives the J504's: macOS's speaker
tuning strips and graphs for the J604's acoustic ID (30, from its ADT)
are byte-identical to those for the J504's (24), and speakersafetyd's
audump.py gives the J504's thermal model from the J604's tuning.
asahi-audio serves the J504 with the J314 FIRs and the J314 microphone
beamformer (aliases-j314), so the J604 uses them too. README.J604.md
records the evidence; no Apple data is added, the comparison is by hash.

Speakers: firs/j604/graph.json is the J314 graph (with its true-peak
limiters) with two differences, as the J616s graph differs from the
J316 one:

- the outputs follow the J604 card's slot order, LW1 RW1 LW2 RW2 LT RT
  (the amps' ADT provider order), not the J314's LW1 RW1 LT RT LW2 RW2;
- both filter nodes set node.pause-on-idle to false, so a paused or
  seeking stream does not leave the convolvers to resume from a cut-off
  state (the #84 pop).

Microphone: mic-j604.json is built from firs/j314/mic.json by
aliases-j314, as mic-j504.json is. The J604's ADT addresses its array
with the J314s's input-data-selectors (1imi2imi3imi).

The cards are hw:AppleJ604 (macaudio "MacBook Pro J604") and
hw:AppleJ604HPAI (aop_audio); the existing AppleJ[0-9]{3} rules already
rename their raw nodes.

The J604 itself has not been measured with a microphone yet.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
