@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# J604 speaker and microphone graphs: evidence
+
+Development reference for Mac16,1 / J604AP (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M4, 2024),
+T8132. Labels: MEASURED (read from the J604 or its macOS), SOURCE (upstream
+files), INFERENCE, TO-VERIFY.
+
+## Why the J604 uses the J314-family graphs
+
+asahi-audio measures each machine and shares FIRs and microphone graphs within
+a tuning family: `make aliases-j314` builds the J414, J504 and J514 (MacBook
+Pro 14-inch, M2 Pro, M3, M3 Pro/Max) graphs and microphone graphs from
+`firs/j314` (Makefile; SOURCE). The J604 belongs to that family by Apple's own
+tuning and by its ADT, not by appearance:
+
+| Fact | Evidence | Label |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| The J604's acoustic ID is 30 | ADT `/product/audio` `acoustic-id` 0x1e, macOS 26B123 and 27.2 | MEASURED |
+| The J504's acoustic ID is 24 | speakersafetyd `docs/speakers.txt` | SOURCE |
+| macOS's speaker tuning for ID 30 equals ID 24 byte for byte | sha256 of `Tunings/AID30/DSP/Strips/builtin_speaker_out_general{,_0,_3}.austrip` and `Graphs/builtin_speaker_out{,_raw}.dspg` equal those of `AID24`; the J604's own 27.2 copy of AID30 has the same hashes | MEASURED |
+| The J604's speakersafetyd model equals the J504's | speakersafetyd `docs/audump.py` on the J604's AID30 tuning gives j504.conf's values section by section | MEASURED |
+| The J604 amps are set up as the J614s/J616s amps are | ADT `audio-speaker` group: `speaker-config`, `bop-config`, `amp-dcblocker-config`, `amp-tx-zd-config` equal the J614s's row for row (26B123, 25G83, RT27.2 and the J604's own boot ADT) | MEASURED |
+| The J604 microphone array is addressed as the J314's | ADT `audio-hp-mic` `input-data-selectors` `1imi2imi3imi` on the J604 (and J614s, J713); `1imi2imi3imi` on the J314s (MacBookPro18,3) | MEASURED / SOURCE |
+
+So Apple drives the J604 speakers with exactly the J504's processing, and the
+J604 graph uses the J504's FIRs, which are the J314 ones. The microphone graph
+is the J314 beamformer, built as `mic-j604.json` by `aliases-j314` like the
+J504's. No Apple data is in this repository: the comparisons are by hash.
+
+## What differs from the J504 speaker graph
+
+- Output order. The J604 card's playback slots follow the amps' ADT provider
+  order, LW1 RW1 LW2 RW2 LT RT (`speaker-config`, the order of the codecs in
+  `t8132-j604.dts`), as on the J616s. The J314/J504 graph is LW1 RW1 LT RT LW2
+  RW2.
+- `node.pause-on-idle` is false on both filter nodes, as in the J616s graph
+  (the #84 resume pop).
+- Everything else, including the true-peak limiters at the end of every path,
+  is the J314 graph as is.
+
+## Open (TO-VERIFY on the J604)
+
+- Upstream practice is to confirm a graph by measurement. The J604 has not
+  been measured with a microphone; the hash identity with the J504 is the
+  strongest evidence short of that.
+- The microphone boosts (7.6 x 7.6) are the J314's. Upstream found the M4 Pro
+  array needs the same order of gain (`1ba7adf`); the J604 level and the
+  beam direction are to be confirmed on speech.
+- Per-unit calibration: macOS fills `speaker-thiele-small` and the mic trims
+  (`syscfg/MiGa`) at run time; these graphs, like every asahi-audio graph, do
+  not use them.
diff --git a/conf/wireplumber.conf b/conf/wireplumber.conf
index 6cb50a3..44ce344 100644
--- a/conf/wireplumber.conf
+++ b/conf/wireplumber.conf
@@ -536,6 +536,30 @@ node.software-dsp.rules = [
         }
     }
 
+    # J604 (MacBook Pro 14", M4, 2024): the J504's tuning family (README.J604.md)
+    {
+        matches = [
+            { api.alsa.path = "hw:AppleJ604,1" }
+        ]
+        actions = {
+            create-filter = {
+                filter-path = "/usr/share/asahi-audio/j604/graph.json"
+                hide-parent = true
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    {
+        matches = [
+            { api.alsa.path = "hw:AppleJ604HPAI,0" }
+        ]
+        actions = {
+            create-filter = {
+                filter-path = "/usr/share/asahi-audio/j314/mic-j604.json"
+                hide-parent = true
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
